  "goodToKnow": "Die Vitrine is a glass display case or cabinet, in museums, shops and living rooms, where many German households keep their best china (das gute Geschirr) for special occasions. It comes from French, ultimately Latin vitrum (glass). In Switzerland, die Vitrine can also mean shop window, which in Germany is das Schaufenster. Plural: die Vitrinen."
